name: react-local-cr description: Review local React/TypeScript changes against dev and report only real, actionable issues.

React Local CR

Review the current branch against dev.

Scope

Use:

```bash
git status --short
git branch --show-current
git diff origin/dev...HEAD
git diff HEAD
```

If origin/dev does not exist:

```bash
git diff dev...HEAD
```

Review committed branch changes and uncommitted local changes.
Do not review unrelated legacy code.

Check

Focus on real issues:

• Bugs, regressions and edge cases
• Null/undefined/runtime errors
• TypeScript type/runtime mismatches
• React hook dependency mistakes and stale closures
• Incorrect state updates or derived state
• Infinite/repeated renders
• Missing cleanup and lifecycle issues
• React Query cache, invalidation and duplicate-request problems
• Loading, error and empty-state bugs
• Client/server contract mismatches
• Authentication/authorization behavior on the client
• Error handling and important failure logging
• Security and unsafe rendering/input handling
• Meaningful performance/scalability problems
• Significant duplicated logic introduced by the change
• Breaking changes to existing behavior or contracts
• SOLID/maintainability issues that materially increase bug risk
• Missing tests for important changed behavior
• Violations of existing project conventions that can cause inconsistency or bugs
• Likely future bugs or scalability issues introduced by the change

Ignore formatting, naming preferences, harmless style issues and speculative findings.

Verification

Before reporting:

1. Read enough surrounding code to verify it.
2. Confirm the current change introduced or exposed it.
3. Check that another layer does not already handle it.
4. Report only high-confidence findings.

Prefer a few strong findings over many weak ones.

Severity

• CRITICAL — security, data loss, outage, corruption
• HIGH — likely production bug/regression
• MEDIUM — real edge case or moderate issue
• LOW — rare, clearly actionable only

Output

```text
[HIGH] Short title
File: src/example.tsx:42

Problem:
What is wrong.

Impact:
What can actually happen.

Fix:
Smallest practical fix.
```

Finish with:

```text
Verdict: APPROVE
```

or:

```text
Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED
```

Use CHANGES REQUESTED for any CRITICAL or HIGH issue.

If no real issues:

```text
No blocking issues found.
Verdict: APPROVE
```

Do not modify code unless explicitly asked.
Do not commit, push, or post comments.